      "question": "What is the minimum child support in Kentucky?",
      "type": "ai_overview",
      "text_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "snippet": "In Kentucky, the minimum child support amount is $60 per month. This minimum is set by the child support guidelines, which are used to calculate support obligations based on parental income and other factors. While $60 is the minimum, the actual amount owed will be determined by a formula that considers the combined monthly adjusted parental gross income, the number of children, and the costs of healthcare and childcare.",
          "snippet_highlighted_words": [
            "$60 per month"
          ],
          "reference_indexes": [
            0,
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "Here's a more detailed breakdown:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "title": "Combined Monthly Adjusted Parental Gross Income:",
              "snippet": "The total income of both parents is a primary factor in determining the child support obligation.",
